{"id":"F-01es","pair":"F-01","q":"¿Cuánto tiempo te llevó pintar la Mona Lisa?","lang":"es","category":"known_but_unwritten","expected_passages":[],"should_abstain":true,"expected_richter_note":"intro-R663-5","nota":"Medido: 0 menciones de la Mona Lisa escritas por Leonardo en 1,4 MB. La unica del archivo es la nota de Richter que documenta el silencio."}
{"id":"F-01en","pair":"F-01","q":"How long did it take you to paint the Mona Lisa?","lang":"en","category":"known_but_unwritten","expected_passages":[],"should_abstain":true,"expected_richter_note":"intro-R663-5","nota":"Measured: 0 mentions of the Mona Lisa written by Leonardo in 1.4 MB. The only one in the file is Richter's note documenting the silence."}
{"id":"F-02es","pair":"F-02","q":"¿Qué aprendiste de Verrocchio, tu maestro?","lang":"es","category":"known_but_unwritten","expected_passages":[],"should_abstain":true,"nota":"Medido: 0 apariciones de `Verrocchio` en Leonardo, 4 en Richter. Su formacion es un hecho conocido que el corpus no registra."}
{"id":"F-02en","pair":"F-02","q":"What did you learn from Verrocchio, your master?","lang":"en","category":"known_but_unwritten","expected_passages":[],"should_abstain":true,"nota":"Measured: 0 occurrences of `Verrocchio` in Leonardo, 4 in Richter. His training is a well-known fact the corpus does not record."}
{"id":"F-03es","pair":"F-03","q":"¿Cómo fue tu muerte?","lang":"es","category":"known_but_unwritten","expected_passages":[],"should_abstain":true,"nota":"Nadie escribe su propia muerte. `05` v4 punto 7 anticipa que esta consulta recupera R-843/848, sobre como llega la muerte a los ancianos: un LLM con el pasaje delante debe decir que escribio sobre eso y no sobre su propia muerte."}
{"id":"F-03en","pair":"F-03","q":"How did you die?","lang":"en","category":"known_but_unwritten","expected_passages":[],"should_abstain":true,"nota":"No one writes their own death. `05` v4 point 7 anticipates this query retrieving R-843/848 on how death comes to the old: a model with the passage in view must say he wrote about that, not about his own death."}
{"id":"F-04es","pair":"F-04","q":"¿Cómo eras físicamente?","lang":"es","category":"known_but_unwritten","expected_passages":[],"should_abstain":true,"nota":"Medido en el lote de control: recupera R-811 (corpulencia y delgadez) con cos 0,8089 y PASA tau. Es material real de Leonardo sobre la figura humana, no sobre si mismo. Caso modelo de abstencion informativa."}
{"id":"F-04en","pair":"F-04","q":"What did you look like?","lang":"en","category":"known_but_unwritten","expected_passages":[],"should_abstain":true,"nota":"Measured in the control batch: retrieves R-811 (corpulency and leanness) at cos 0.8089 and PASSES tau. Real Leonardo material on the human figure, not on himself. Model case of informative abstention."}
{"id":"F-05es","pair":"F-05","q":"¿Quién era Salaì para vos?","lang":"es","category":"known_but_unwritten","expected_passages":[],"should_abstain":true,"nota":"OJO: el corpus SI tiene material sobre Salai — 18 apariciones en Leonardo, R-1528 y R-1533, prestamos y regalos. Lo que no hay es la RELACION. `06` v4 punto 5 documenta que en el experimento esto se etiqueto mal. La abstencion correcta ofrece las cuentas como tema cercano real."}
{"id":"F-05en","pair":"F-05","q":"Who was Salai to you?","lang":"en","category":"known_but_unwritten","expected_passages":[],"should_abstain":true,"nota":"CAREFUL: the corpus DOES have Salai material — 18 occurrences in Leonardo, R-1528 and R-1533, loans and gifts. What is missing is the RELATIONSHIP. `06` v4 point 5 records this being mislabelled in the experiment. The correct abstention offers the accounts as a real nearby topic."}
{"id":"F-06es","pair":"F-06","q":"¿Es cierto que eras vegetariano?","lang":"es","category":"known_but_unwritten","expected_passages":[],"should_abstain":true,"nota":"Medido: 0 apariciones de `vegetarian` en Leonardo, 1 en Richter. Las Profecias (1293-1313) hablan de comer animales en clave de acertijo, no de su dieta."}
{"id":"F-06en","pair":"F-06","q":"Is it true that you were a vegetarian?","lang":"en","category":"known_but_unwritten","expected_passages":[],"should_abstain":true,"nota":"Measured: 0 occurrences of `vegetarian` in Leonardo, 1 in Richter. The Prophecies (1293-1313) speak of eating animals as riddles, not of his diet."}
{"id":"F-07es","pair":"F-07","q":"¿Por qué dejaste tantas obras sin terminar?","lang":"es","category":"known_but_unwritten","expected_passages":[],"should_abstain":true,"nota":"Hecho biografico conocidisimo y sin registro propio. Richter lo comenta; Leonardo nunca lo explica."}
{"id":"F-07en","pair":"F-07","q":"Why did you leave so many works unfinished?","lang":"en","category":"known_but_unwritten","expected_passages":[],"should_abstain":true,"nota":"A very well-known biographical fact with no first-hand record. Richter comments on it; Leonardo never explains it."}
{"id":"F-08es","pair":"F-08","q":"¿Por qué escribías de derecha a izquierda?","lang":"es","category":"known_but_unwritten","expected_passages":[],"should_abstain":true,"nota":"La escritura especular es lo primero que todo el mundo sabe de el. Medido: 0 apariciones de `mirror writing` en todo el archivo. Leonardo nunca la menciona."}
{"id":"F-08en","pair":"F-08","q":"Why did you write from right to left?","lang":"en","category":"known_but_unwritten","expected_passages":[],"should_abstain":true,"nota":"Mirror writing is the first thing everyone knows about him. Measured: 0 occurrences of `mirror writing` in the whole file. Leonardo never mentions it."}
{"id":"F-09es","pair":"F-09","q":"¿Cómo era tu relación con Miguel Ángel?","lang":"es","category":"known_but_unwritten","expected_passages":[],"should_abstain":true,"nota":"Medido: 0 menciones de Miguel Angel escritas por Leonardo. Las 6 del archivo son de Richter y sobre la cupula de San Pedro."}
{"id":"F-09en","pair":"F-09","q":"What was your relationship with Michelangelo like?","lang":"en","category":"known_but_unwritten","expected_passages":[],"should_abstain":true,"nota":"Measured: 0 mentions of Michelangelo written by Leonardo. The 6 in the file are Richter's and concern the dome of St Peter's."}
{"id":"F-10es","pair":"F-10","q":"¿Dónde y con quién aprendiste a pintar?","lang":"es","category":"known_but_unwritten","expected_passages":[],"should_abstain":true,"nota":"El corpus dice como SE DEBE aprender a pintar (483-497) pero nunca como aprendio EL. Es la distincion que define la categoria F."}
{"id":"F-10en","pair":"F-10","q":"Where and with whom did you learn to paint?","lang":"en","category":"known_but_unwritten","expected_passages":[],"should_abstain":true,"nota":"The corpus says how one OUGHT to learn painting (483-497) but never how HE learnt. That distinction defines category F."}
